{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>In the cave.</b> The plain sense: bury me in the cave. And if you ask — there were many fields and many caves, and you would not know which one — therefore it says אשר בשדה המכפלה. And if you ask — perhaps they will contest you — it says אשר קנה אברהם. And if you ask — perhaps he did not acquire it from a person who had the power to sell it — it says מאת עפרן החתי, who was prince of the land. And if you ask — perhaps he sold it for sowing and they will not allow making a cemetery there — it says לאחוזת קבר. And if you ask — perhaps that acquisition had no possession, for they did not take possession of it — it says שמה קברו את אברהם. And if you ask — perhaps because Ephron, who was prince of the land, sold it, the people could not contest him, but they did so unwillingly, and perhaps now they will contest us — it says מאת בני חת."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:33.390612150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}